## APPENDIX D – INTEGRATION WITH AI SAFETY ECOSYSTEM

### D.1 FamilyGuard Voice Integrity Integration

**Purpose:** Combine hardware kill (YUVA-9V) with voice-activated emergency shutdown.

**Architecture:**

```
Child Voice Detection (iPhone/Device)
         │
         ├─ 20dB spike detected
         ├─ Child voice frequency (300-3000Hz)
         ├─ Fear/panic tone (FFT analysis)
         │
         ▼
   [FamilyGuard App]
         │
         ├─ Local decision (no cloud)
         ├─ Sends kill signal via:
         │   - WiFi to YUVA-9V watchdog input
         │   - Bluetooth fallback
         │   - Cellular (if enabled)
         │
         ▼
   [YUVA-9V Opto Input]
         │
         ├─ Light goes DARK
         ├─ Latch trips (74HC14)
         ├─ Contactor opens
         │
         ▼
   AI COMPUTE POWER OFF

Alternative: Direct Hardware Integration
   [FamilyGuard Device] ──3.5mm audio jack──> [YUVA-9V Trigger Input]
         │
         ├─ Audio signal >threshold
         ├─ Comparator (LM393)
         ├─ Opto input darkens
         │
         ▼
   IMMEDIATE KILL (<50ms latency)
```

**Implementation Notes:**

- FamilyGuard runs on-device (iPhone, dedicated hardware)
- No cloud dependency; works offline
- YUVA-9V watchdog input accepts:
  - 3.3V logic signal (active-high, kill-on-low)
  - Opto-isolated (HCPL-817)
  - Audio threshold trigger (analog fallback)

**Installation:**

1. Configure FamilyGuard with YUVA-9V IP address (local network only)
1. OR: Wire 3.5mm audio output to YUVA-9V analog trigger input
1. Test kill sequence: Simulate 20dB spike → verify <1 second shutdown
1. Document in chain-of-custody log

